elf into thinking that that's  actually true yeah but you have to  listen to your inner voice and if you  find a spark if you're really fall in  love with a person the fact that she is  too beautiful for you or a language  being too hard doesn't count anymore  that's what really counts and in order  to ignite that spark you have to find a  reason if you haven't found a solid  reason or solid reasons keep looking for  me one of the the things that push me  towards a language is not so much as how  it sounds that it does help its grammar  and stuff it's more about the  experiences that I have the things that  are represented by the language to me go  visit in the country and talking to  people and having experiences is the  most important thing even before the the  language itself and it really depends on  the individual to be that for you  reading a book of history of that  country or like you like the food or you  talk to a person can be the igniting  spark and everybody is different but  once again you have to keep looking and  you have to know exactly why you want to  embark on this romantic story  this is absolutely important and another  thing is that it's a long it's a  long-term project so to say it's a  long-term quest so you have to give it  daily care and so much as you give daily  care to your partner you have to  understand how to give daily care to a  language in order to do that you have to  have some kind of plan you have to have  some kind of objective long-term goals  and for example for me Hungarian my  long-term goal is I want to reach  fluency in two years now what I what do  I mean by fluency fluency is a very  subjective term it if you want to see  it's clear the important things that  it's clear for me I give myself a  definition of fluence that you can check  my article about how to region 8 like  fluency to see what basic fluency in  fluency are for me and so if I have this  goal in two years I also can imagine my  trip backwards and I can think okay my  midterm goal is to reach basic fluency  one year and my short term goal is to  finish as Emil in four months and they  set a date so I have to start  point I have the final destination and I  can't imagine may trip backwards I  started learning and garen officially on  the 4th of December and I'm sorry for  the 4th of November and from that moment  on I knew that I would learn and give  data care to to Hungarian and also you  have to know how to keep this this love  story going so knowing exactly why is  the first step but you also have to know  how to deal with that so even if I'm  Goering is supposed to be a very hard  language is quite different from Italian  for my native Italian I know how exactly  how to deal with that because I apply my  method which is called bilingual I  called bilingual translation which I'm  applying to a gear and I'm having a  blast with it because I'm learning  faster than I have ever done with with  any other language so just to recap  falling in love with the language it's  like falling in love with a person it  follows some some important rules you  have to understand exactly why it  doesn't have to be just an infatuation  otherwise it might turn into some kind  of summer fling which disappears very  quickly and in order for the love story  to continue have to give it daily care  you have to know where you're going and  you have to know how you're going there  and to finish this  I wanted to quote Gary Chapman who said  that love is a choice that we make every  single day thanks for listening
 

